# Next.js rules

- Before editing Next.js code, read the relevant version-matched docs in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` where available.
- Prefer Server Components by default. Add `"use client"` only at the smallest interactive boundary.
- Use a server-only Data Access Layer (DAL) for reads and writes. DAL functions must enforce authorization and return minimal DTOs.
- Treat Server Actions and Route Handlers as public request boundaries: validate input, authenticate, authorize, resolve tenant, rate-limit where appropriate, and return safe errors.
- Do not place business rules in React components, route files, or Server Actions. Delegate to application use cases.
- Do not import database clients, secrets, or server-only packages into client components.
- Keep cache behavior explicit. Never cache private tenant data across users/tenants without a proven cache key and isolation test.
